    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the properties of a triangle's interior angles:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the mean value:**\n   The mean value is found by dividing the sum of the angles by the number of angles (which is 3 in this case).\n\nLet's go through the calculations step by step:\n\n1. **Sum of the interior angles:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum} = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Number of angles:**\n   A triangle has 3 interior angles.\n\n3. **Calculate the mean:**\n   The mean value is calculated by dividing the sum of the angles by the number of angles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of the angles}}{\\text{Number of angles}} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
