    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the sum of the interior angles of a triangle:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always 180 degrees. This is a fundamental property of triangles.\n\n2. **Set up the equation for the mean:**\n   The mean (average) of the measures of the three interior angles can be calculated by dividing the sum of the angles by the number of angles. Since there are three angles, we divide 180 degrees by 3.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of the angles}}{\\text{Number of angles}} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
