      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we can use the fact that the sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is always 180 degrees.\n\nLet's denote the measures of the three interior angles of the triangle as A, B, and C.\n\nWe know that:\nA + B + C = 180 degrees\n\nNow, to find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles, we need to divide the sum of the angles by the number of angles, which is 3.\n\nMean value = (A + B + C) / 3\n\nSubstituting the given sum of the angles:\n\nMean value = 180 degrees / 3\n\nMean value = 60 degrees\n\nSo, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is 60 degrees.",
