      "sample_index": 7,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the properties of a triangle's angles:**\n   - The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the mean value:**\n   - The mean value is the sum of the angles divided by the number of angles.\n\nLet's denote the measures of the three interior angles of the triangle as \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\).\n\n3. **Sum of the angles:**\n   \\[\n   A + B + C = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. **Number of angles:**\n   - There are 3 angles in a triangle.\n\n5. **Calculate the mean:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean} = \\frac{A + B + C}{3}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Substitute the sum of the angles:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean} = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
